## 🚀 How to Deploy to Vercel in 2 Minutes

### Method 1: Deploy via GitHub (Recommended & Easiest)

1. **Create a GitHub Repository**:
   - Go to [GitHub.com](https://github.com) and create a new public or private repository (e.g., `dilshad-portfolio`).
2. **Upload Files**:
   - Click **"Upload an existing file"** on your new repository page.
   - Drag and drop all the files from this folder (`index.html`, `vercel.json`, `package.json`, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `Md_Dilshad_Uddin_Taj_CV.pdf`, `dilshad_taj_bw_portrait.jpg`).
   - Commit the changes.
3. **Connect to Vercel**:
   - Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) and sign in (you can sign in with your GitHub account).
   - Click **"Add New..."** &rarr; **"Project"**.
   - Select your `dilshad-portfolio` repository and click **"Import"**.
   - Leave all default settings as-is (Framework: *Other*, Root Directory: `./`).
   - Click **"Deploy"**.

Your portfolio will be live in ~20 seconds with a free production URL (e.g., `https://dilshad-portfolio.vercel.app`) with automatic SSL, worldwide CDN, and instantaneous caching!

---

### Method 2: Deploy via Terminal (Vercel CLI)

If you have Node.js installed, open PowerShell or Terminal in this folder and run:

```bash
npx vercel
```

- Log in when prompted.
- Set up and deploy: press `Y`.
- Accept all default settings by pressing `Enter`.
- For production deployment:
  ```bash
  npx vercel --prod
  ```

